Hisense A6L audio-20261010 r3 (10 Oct 2026, firmware/extracted/audio-20261010) for the AOSP AIDL example audio HAL
(StreamPrimary): the primary playback PCM follows the MultiMedia1 DSP back end. a6l-audio-route selects TERT_MI2S_RX
(loudspeaker) or LPI_MI2S_RX_0 (WCD codec: wired headset, earpiece) from vendor.a6l.audio.media_out; q6routing binds the
ADM COPP to the back end selected at PCM prepare and never moves a running session. Live 10 Oct: a speaker ->
headphones switch under a running PCM made every pcm_write fail until standby, a headphones -> speaker switch left the
speaker silent. When the selected back end differs from the one the PCM was opened on, the PCM is closed and reopened.
Off switch: vendor.a6l.audio.media_follow_be=false (not persistent). Apply after 0001-0006, in hardware/interfaces, by
tools/rom-v2-pipeline.sh (audio/patches/*.patch).

